hexagon: enable the HVX IEEE float instructions on v73 and v75

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The HVX IEEE float instructions (vadd, vsub and vmpy on sf and hf, and the
widening vmpy of hf into sf) exist in the ISA from v68. The compiler enables
them on v79 and a subsequent version. On v73 and v75 they are an option,
-mhvx-ieee-fp, that is off. Before this change the v75 link stopped with
"Cannot select: intrinsic %llvm.hexagon.V6.vmpy.sf.hf.128B", thus the series
did not build for any core before v79.

With the option, libggml-htp-v73.so and libggml-htp-v75.so build. They hold
29 IEEE instructions in 5 functions: softmax_job_f32 (12 vmpy sf, 12 vadd sf),
gdn_conv_band_packed_4 and _1 (4 vmpy hf into sf) and gdn_ch_phase_a (1 vsub
sf). Every other float instruction takes the qf path of upstream.

Verified on hexagon-sim of the toolchain image on 2026-09-22: on the v73 and
the v75 core models, vadd, vsub and vmpy of sf and hf and vmpy of hf into sf
agree bit for bit with the scalar IEEE unit, over 12800 to 25600 lanes each,
with zeros, infinities, NaN, subnormals and cancellation in the inputs.

Not verified on silicon. Qualcomm's own IEEE float library (QHL, the _af
functions) uses only qf instructions on these cores. If a part does not have
the option, the first of these 29 instructions stops the DSP session. Run
test-backend-ops on a v75 phone before a release depends on this patch.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/CMakeLists.txt

How to apply, from the llama.cpp root:

    git apply patches/hexagon-ieee-pre79/0001-hexagon-htp-enable-hvx-ieee-fp-on-v73-and-v75.patch

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/CMakeLists.txt b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/CMakeLists.txt
index 3382ca0..d93c940 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -52,6 +52,12 @@ target_compile_definitions(${HTP_LIB} PRIVATE
     $<IF:$<BOOL:${HEXAGON_HTP_DEBUG}>,HTP_DEBUG=1,NDEBUG=1>
     $<IF:$<BOOL:${HEXAGON_HTP_DEBUG}>,FARF_HIGH=1,>)
 
+# v73 and v75 have the HVX IEEE float instructions as an option that the compiler does not enable, v79 enables them.
+if(DSP_VERSION STREQUAL "v73" OR DSP_VERSION STREQUAL "v75")
+    target_compile_options(${HTP_LIB} PRIVATE -mhvx-ieee-fp)
+    target_link_options(${HTP_LIB} PRIVATE -mhvx-ieee-fp)
+endif()
+
 
 build_idl(htp_iface.idl ${HTP_LIB})
 
